Mike Kelly wrote:
> Same race sacrifice as a chaotic always successfully converts.

	Same-race sacrifice always converts the altar, regardless of
your alignment. If you're not chaotic, though, what it converts it to is
probably not what you were after. It summons demons, too, which are
hostile if you're not chaotic.

> Do not try to convert unaligned altars (Moloch altars).

	Actually, the rule is: Don't try to convert altars in Gehennom.
Unaligned altars outside Gehennom (there are a few in various Quests)
convert just fine.

	Don't try to convert altars with unicorns that match your
alignment *or the alignment of the altar*. It might seem like it'd be
extra-effective to convert a lawful altar using a white unicorn, but
what it mostly does is seriously piss off the original owner of the
altar.

